
\[P(F^{\prime}|_{\text{r}_{1}},\text{r}_{2},\uplambda) = e^{\frac{\uplambda}{2}(1 - \underline{\tau})}x^{\frac{\uplambda}{2}(\nu_{1}+\nu_{2}-2)}\sum\limits_{l = 0}^{\frac{\nu_{2}}{2}-1}T_{i}\quad(\text{r}_{2}\text{ even})\]

where

\(T_{0} = 1\)

\(T_{1} = \frac{1}{2}(\nu_{1} + \nu_{2} - 2 + \uplambda x)\frac{1 - \underline{\tau}}{\underline{\tau}}\)

\(T_{i} = \frac{1 - \underline{\tau}}{2\underline{i}}\left[(\nu_{1} + \nu_{2} - 2i + \uplambda x)T_{i - 1} + \uplambda(1 - \underline{\tau})T_{i - 2}\right]\)

\(x = \frac{\nu_{2}}{\nu_{1}F^{\prime} + \nu_{2}}\)

\(\lim\limits_{\nu \to 0}P(F^{\prime}|_{\text{r}_{1}},\text{r}_{2},\uplambda) = P(\chi^{\prime 2}|_{\text{r}},\uplambda)\),

\(\chi^{\prime 2} = \nu_{1}F^{\prime}\), \(\underline{\nu = \nu_{1}}\)

\(\lim\limits_{\nu \to 0}P(F^{\prime}|_{\text{r}_{1}},\text{r}_{2},\uplambda) = Q(\chi^{2}|_{\text{r}})\),

\(\chi^{2} = \frac{\nu_{1}(1 + c^{2})}{F^{\prime}}\)

where \(\uplambda/\nu_{1} \to c^{\text{a}}\) as \(\nu_{1} \to c\) .

